{"year":"2022","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 79th edition, on January 9, 2022, was the first without a traditional ceremony since 2008 and the first without a TV broadcast since 1979. Amid the boycott by studios, artists and NBC itself of the Hollywood Foreign Press Association (HFPA), criticized for the lack of diversity among its members, the awards were handed out at a private event at the Beverly Hilton, with no nominees, guests or press, and the winners were announced via press release and on social media. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 600583, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Power of the Dog</a> (2021) won Best Motion Picture – Drama and Director (<a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 10757, 'screen_type': person}\">Jane Campion</a>), and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 511809, 'screen_type': movie}\">West Side Story</a> (2021) took Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy. At 20, <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 2217977, 'screen_type': person}\">Rachel Zegler</a> became the youngest winner of Best Actress in a Musical or Comedy. <i>Television awards are not included.</i>"},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Motion Picture – Drama","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":600583,"name":"The Power of the Dog","image_path":"/rgDJDLFKOKF0dpbaVwgbvjbyZgM.jpg","director":"Jane Campion","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/gAsHuCQMN7mv4uFIvM4ACQ09hPr.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":777270,"name":"Belfast","image_path":"/3mInLZyPOVLsZRsBwNHi3UJXXnm.jpg","director":"Kenneth Branagh","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":776503,"name":"CODA","image_path":"/fXeWSHLlAEsINva6SJgb5hCLBzy.jpg","director":"Sian Heder","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":438631,"name":"Dune","image_path":"/uzERcfV2rSHNhW5eViQiO9hNiA7.jpg","director":"Denis Villeneuve","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":614917,"name":"King Richard","image_path":"/KUdG6W99PfHe3wzuBWgfsHUuM.jpg","director":"Reinaldo Marcus Green","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","n